{
  "scene_id": "scene06_taxonomy",
  "video_title": "What Is Machine Learning?",
  "scene_title": "The Taxonomy of the Field",
  "order": 6,
  "duration_mode": "audio_driven",
  "voice": {
    "language": "en-IN",
    "speaker": "priya",
    "model": "bulbul:v3"
  },
  "narration": [
    {
      "id": "s6_01",
      "text": "Machine learning is not one single technique."
    },
    {
      "id": "s6_02",
      "text": "The four main categories are: supervised learning, unsupervised learning, semi-supervised learning, reinforcement learning."
    },
    {
      "id": "s6_03",
      "text": "The first is supervised learning. This is the most common form."
    },
    {
      "id": "s6_04",
      "text": "For example, if we want to classify emails as spam or not spam, we train the model on labeled examples."
    },
    {
      "id": "s6_05",
      "text": "The second is unsupervised learning. Here, there are no labels."
    },
    {
      "id": "s6_06",
      "text": "The model only sees the data and tries to find structure on its own. It might discover clusters, groups, or hidden patterns."
    },
    {
      "id": "s6_07",
      "text": "This is useful when we do not already know what categories exist."
    },
    {
      "id": "s6_08",
      "text": "The third is semi-supervised learning. This is a mix of the two."
    },
    {
      "id": "s6_09",
      "text": "We have a small amount of labeled data and a large amount of unlabeled data. The labeled examples help guide the learning process."
    },
    {
      "id": "s6_10",
      "text": "This is useful because labels can be expensive to create."
    },
    {
      "id": "s6_11",
      "text": "The fourth is reinforcement learning. Here, the model learns by interacting with an environment."
    },
    {
      "id": "s6_12",
      "text": "It takes actions, receives rewards or penalties, and learns which actions lead to better outcomes."
    },
    {
      "id": "s6_13",
      "text": "This is how systems can learn strategies over time."
    }
  ],
